(HMBPP, 5-OP-RU) [P0444]. Treg/Th17 balance [P0098, P0154].\\n    *   **Unit 03:**\\n        *   Barrier integrity. Gut-on-chip evidence (responders vs non-responders) [P0073]. Dual role of bacteria (P. bifermentans) [P0284].\\n        *   Translocation. Active transport via DCs to MLN/Tumor [P0166]. Not just leaky gut. PDAC context [P0084].\\n        *   Myeloid reprogramming. TAM/MDSC phenotype shifts [P0084, P0362].\\n        *   Human context. FMT-LUMINate safety/efficacy context (Prevotella toxicity in dual ICI) [P0583].\\n    *   **Unit 04:**\\n        *   Tumor specificity. Melanoma vs NSCLC vs GI vs Prostate (Akkermansia reversal) [P0270, P0352].\\n        *   Model differences. Mouse causality vs Human correlation [P0535, P0146].\\n        *   Table: Summarize tumor types, key microbes, mechanisms, evidence type.\\n    *   **Closing:** Transition to Ch3 (Metabolites).\\n\\n5.  **Refining Constraints:**\\n    *   Check source usage: Ensure P0080 is used for LPS, P0114 for DC, P0242 for PD-L2, P0388 for mimicry, P0444 for metabolites/T cells, P0073/P0284 for barrier, P0166 for translocation, P0583 for human context/toxicity, P0270/P0352 for specificity.\\n    *   Check tone: Avoid overclaiming causality in humans. Use phrases like \\\"animal models suggest,\\\" \\\"human cohorts show association.\\\"\\n    *   Check formatting: Markdown headers, proper citation style [Pxxxx].\\n    *   Check Metadata: List all Ch2 task IDs as completed.\\n\\n6.  **Writing - Section by Section (Mental Draft):**\\n    *   *Intro:* Ch1 showed *that* microbiome matters. Ch2 explains *how*.\\n    *   *U01:* Start with PRRs. LPS structure (hexa-acylated) matters more than just LPS presence [P0080]. Then DCs. Ruminococcaceae strain drives CD103+ DCs via TLR/IRF8 [P0114]. Then PD-L2 modulation [P0242].\\n    *   *U02:* T cells. Mimicry (SFB antigen) [P0388]. Metabolites (DAT, HMBPP) affecting T cell priming/exhaustion [P0195, P0444].\\n    *   *U03:* Barrier. Chip model shows non-responder feces damage barrier [P0073]. Translocation is active (DC-mediated) [P0166]. Myeloid cells are the endpoint [P0084]. Human FMT shows context-dependent toxicity [P0583].\\n    *   *U04:* Specificity. Prostate (Akkermansia negative) [P0270]. Lung (respiratory microbiome) [P0352]. Table.\\n    *   *Conclusion:* Mechanisms are clear in mice, complex in humans. Next chapter focuses on metabolites.\\n\\n7.  **Final Review against Instructions:**\\n    *   Did I repeat Ch1? No.\\n    *   Did I use the sources correctly? Yes.\\n    *   Is the metadata correct? Yes.\\n    *   Is the language scientific Chinese? Yes.\\n    *   Is the flow logical? Yes.\\n\\n    *Self-Correction on Metadata:* The `completed_task_ids` should only include the tasks *actually completed in this response*. Since I am writing the whole of Chapter 2 in this window (based on `current_task_ids` covering all Ch2 tasks), I will list all Ch2 task IDs.\\n\\n    *Wait, one check on `current_task_ids`:* It lists all Ch2 tasks. I should aim to complete all of them in this response if possible within token limits, or at least a coherent substantial portion. Given the depth required, I will write the full Chapter 2 content as per the `current_task_ids` list.\\n\\n    *Wait, another check on `accepted_body_markdown`:* It ends with the Table from Chapter 1. I need to start immediately with Chapter 2 Title.\\n\\n    *Citation Style:* The prompt uses `[P0080]` format in the source briefs. I will use this format.\\n\\n    *Specific Source Details:*\\n    *   P0080: Hexa-acylated LPS, TLR4, melanoma/MC38.\\n    *   P0114: Ruminococcaceae, CD103+ DC, IRF8, NFATc1.\\n    *   P0242: C. cateniformis, PD-L2/RGMb, MYD88.\\n    *   P0388: SFB, molecular mimicry, Th17 to Th1-like.\\n    *   P0444: MEP pathway, HMBPP, Vδ2 T cells, Riboflavin, MAIT.\\n    *   P0073: Gut-on-chip, barrier integrity, LPS vs Flagellin.\\n    *   P0166: Bacterial translocation, DC-mediated, MLN.\\n    *   P0583: FMT-LUMINate, Prevotella toxi